<title>JAPAN: Japan, U.S. firms to join Pakistan power project.</title>
<headline>Japan, U.S. firms to join Pakistan power project.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissho Iwai Corp said on Friday that it and two U.S. firms would take part in a $150 million project to build and operate a power plant in Pakistan for Saba Power Company Ltd.</p>
<p>The Japanese trading house, Coastal Power Co and Cogen Technologies will manage the project, which will involve construction of a 125-megawatt fuel oil power generator in Sheikupura, Punjab, Nissho Iwai said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant is due to start operations in April 1999 and will provide electricity to Pakistan's state-run Water and Power Development Authority (WAPDA) under a 30-year contract, it said.</p>
